+//  - checkpoint_mem writes the usual VeloC file image (header + regions) as ONE stream into a cxlpath
+//    object; no scratch file, no DRAM staging copy. The drain target is the file VeloC would have
+//    produced in `persistent`, so stock VeloC can restart from it after a reboot.
